      "author": "Participant 1",
      "body": "Trying to connect directly to the backend server without https. Same behavior and error massages... as reported here: #14184 

Tested Browsers on Mac OS: Safari, Firefox"
    },
    {
      "id": 384427625,
      "url": "https://github.com/phpmyadmin/phpmyadmin/issues/14219#issuecomment-384427625",
      "created_at": "2018-04-25T20:43:34Z",
      "updated_at": "2018-04-26T15:36:45Z",
      "author": "Participant 2",
      "body": "The problem is that the cookies are restricted by a defined path :
```
Set-Cookie: phpMyAdmin=cjnp37dge73th23009kvnm2k63; path=/phpmyadmin/; HttpOnly
Set-Cookie: pma_lang=en; expires=Fri, 25-May-2018 20:30:44 GMT; Max-Age=2592000; path=/phpmyadmin/; HttpOnly
```

If you add a cookie path rewriter in one of the 2 location blocks : `proxy_cookie_path /phpmyadmin/ /;`
The login succeeds.
 
See on nginx docs : [here](http://nginx.org/en/docs/http/ngx_http_proxy_module.html#proxy_cookie_path)

[EDIT] Issue fixed on Stackoverflow, solution accepted.

"
